---
// Tetlock (2007): high media pessimism predicts downward price pressure followed by a reversion to
// fundamentals. Two competing readings of a gloomy column are drawn as stylised price paths:
// "it was news" (a step that stays) and "it was mood" (a dip that comes back). The paper's tests
// favour the second. Shapes only; no data points.
const W = 900;
const H = 340;
---
<figure class="p17t">
  <div class="p17t-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Two stylised price paths after a gloomy newspaper column. If the column carried real news, the price would step down and stay there. If it only reflected mood, the price would dip and then return to where it was. Tetlock's tests on the Wall Street Journal column Abreast of the Market found the second pattern: pessimism predicts downward pressure followed by reversion.">
    <text x="20" y="28" class="p17t-h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>A gloomy column: new information, or just mood?</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Một cột báo ảm đạm: thông tin mới, hay chỉ là tâm trạng?</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="20" y="48" width="420" height="230" rx="8" class="p17t-panel" />
    <text x="36" y="72" class="p17t-t">
      <tspan data-lang-en>If the text was news</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Nếu văn bản là tin tức</tspan>
    </text>
    <line x1="40" y1="150" x2="420" y2="150" class="p17t-ref" />
    <path d="M 40 150 L 190 150 L 200 205 L 420 205" class="p17t-path" fill="none" />
    <line x1="195" y1="248" x2="195" y2="100" class="p17t-tick" />
    <text x="40" y="262" class="p17t-s">
      <tspan data-lang-en>the price steps down and stays</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>giá bước xuống và ở lại đó</tspan>
    </text>

    <rect x="460" y="48" width="420" height="230" rx="8" class="p17t-panel is-found" />
    <text x="476" y="72" class="p17t-t">
      <tspan data-lang-en>If the text was mood (what Tetlock found)</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Nếu văn bản là tâm trạng (điều Tetlock thấy)</tspan>
    </text>
    <line x1="480" y1="150" x2="860" y2="150" class="p17t-ref" />
    <path d="M 480 150 L 630 150 L 640 205 C 670 214, 700 190, 740 160 C 760 150, 800 150, 860 150" class="p17t-path is-found" fill="none" />
    <line x1="635" y1="248" x2="635" y2="100" class="p17t-tick" />
    <text x="480" y="262" class="p17t-s">
      <tspan data-lang-en>pessimism, then downward pressure, then reversion</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>bi quan, rồi áp lực giảm, rồi hồi về</tspan>
    </text>

    <text x="20" y="312" class="p17t-note">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Stylised shapes, not data. The vertical line marks the day the column appears.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Các hình dạng được vẽ lại cho gọn, không phải số liệu. Đường dọc đánh dấu ngày cột báo xuất hiện.</tspan>
    </text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Tetlock (2007) scored the Wall Street Journal column "Abreast of the Market" for pessimism, 1984 to 1999. Reversal is what separates mood from news.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Tetlock (2007) chấm điểm bi quan cho cột "Abreast of the Market" của Wall Street Journal, 1984 đến 1999. Việc giá hồi về là thứ phân biệt tâm trạng với tin tức.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .p17t { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .p17t-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .p17t svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .p17t text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .p17t .p17t-h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .p17t .p17t-t { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .p17t .p17t-s { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .p17t .p17t-note { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .p17t-panel { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .p17t-panel.is-found { stroke: var(--gold-icon); stroke-width: 1.6; }
  .p17t-ref { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 4 4; }
  .p17t-path { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 2.2; }
  .p17t-path.is-found { stroke: var(--gold-icon); }
  .p17t-tick { stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1; stroke-dasharray: 3 3; }
  .p17t figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
